<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Pick Lock</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Thief (guild level 2)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>pick &lt;door or thing&gt;
pick &lt;direction&gt; &lt;door&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>pick door
pick chest
</pre>
<p>A fast way past a locked door or chest when you have no key: you work the 
lock until it gives with a soft *click*. A picked door is unlocked on 
both sides.
</p><p>Your skill and your dexterity decide it, against how hard the lock is: 
some locks are much harder than others, and some can't be picked at all 
("This door seems to be pick proof"). A failed try costs you endurance, 
more the worse you failed, and you can try again. You must be standing.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Lock</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Open</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Thief Skills</a>
</pre>




</div>